{"title":"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(credit_to_crazyfehmy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (credit to crazyfehmy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(credit_to_dskull16)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (credit to dskull16)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be two positive integers. If there are infinitely many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c09284db6d553ac0881a04a8d017b930aee15f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2+2kn+m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square, prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec4f3da4f422b2346efe86724c8a0aee1023fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28credit_to_crazyfehmy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(credit_to_crazyfehmy)\">Solution 1 (credit to crazyfehmy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (credit to crazyfehmy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that we can <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Completing_the_square\" title=\"Completing the square\">complete the square</a> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1f06202b3843fc9ab4bfab033c08d81a694a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + 2kn + n^2 - n^2 + m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" />, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb92b26cc71fafb47fc682db6c061346e582d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAssume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0b58b81ad8d1281aaf0c31d8bf23d6e26cf24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> are positive, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b0d68813175189775215505b81b7569f1851ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - n^2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />.  In order to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb92b26cc71fafb47fc682db6c061346e582d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> is not a perfect square, we can show that there are values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a6cc4f9890e947cfc0fa523b6dee47152b10154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 &lt; (k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2 &lt; (k+n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"358\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b0d68813175189775215505b81b7569f1851ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - n^2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0e87da0b6bfe39bb452d64428a8c2cb37b9a27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 &lt; (k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" />.  In the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf9edf07dd95729d5cbd6feb45324e67290981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2 &lt; (k+n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"269\" height=\"19\" />, we can expand and simplify to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7e1e96d9cdbc01574ee782bec01e21a9c63935e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} k^2 + 2kn + n^2 + m^2 - n^2 &amp;&lt; k^2 + 2kn + n^2 + 2k + 2n + 1 \\\\ m^2 - n^2 &amp;&lt; 2k + 2n + 1 \\\\ \\frac{m^2 - n^2 - 2n - 1}{2} &amp;&lt; k. \\end{align*}\" width=\"444\" height=\"94\" />\nAll steps are reversible, so there are values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a6cc4f9890e947cfc0fa523b6dee47152b10154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 &lt; (k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2 &lt; (k+n+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"358\" height=\"19\" />, so there are no values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0b58b81ad8d1281aaf0c31d8bf23d6e26cf24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" /> that results in infinite number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy the original conditions.\n</p><p><br />\nNow assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2142770fa24b44536073e58e97ca948a989965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> are positive, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31aca61f38eb65907bfeb547a9d6f436a481bb15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - n^2 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />.  In order to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb92b26cc71fafb47fc682db6c061346e582d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> is not a perfect square, we can show that there are values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/7/fe7c5bc17cbf565c966bd46502a9b3c35f7e71e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n-1)^2 &lt; (k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2 &lt; (k+n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"359\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31aca61f38eb65907bfeb547a9d6f436a481bb15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - n^2 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/773fab0aa2bd274b00ad57c4ff218eed32b8a528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2 &lt; (k+n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" />.  In the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9783da910500d582f4754ca0e6d3a08dd3fee86d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n-1)^2 &lt; (k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"19\" />, we can expand and simplify to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1afe98f710a85b0a128e2af95286d2cc0b3b82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} k^2 + 2kn + n^2 - 2k - 2n + 1 &amp;&lt; k^2 + 2kn + n^2 + m^2 - n^2 \\\\ -2k - 2n + 1 &amp;&lt; m^2 - n^2 \\\\ k &amp;&gt; -\\frac{m^2 - n^2 + 2n - 1}{2}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"443\" height=\"94\" />\nAll steps are reversible, so there are values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9783da910500d582f4754ca0e6d3a08dd3fee86d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n-1)^2 &lt; (k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"19\" />, so there are no values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6851ca945f78b10a85c14fc57fbaf75e69f57241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b2142770fa24b44536073e58e97ca948a989965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" /> that results in infinite number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy the original conditions.\n</p><p><br />\nNow we need to prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39526a4fd8fa70a09be9251b26dbfb4bb423219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" />, there are an infinite number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfy the original conditions.  By the Substitution Property, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e0a0b9df30f40b13a7bf5c84cc198d0e924040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + 2kn + m^2 = k^2 + 2kn + n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" />.  The expression can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a4dbb9cabc002c204d2a34625d01b20056ab44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" />.  Since the expression is a perfect square, for all integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cff91106986d596b444b21427ff9ee5ac08db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n, k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"16\" />, there are an infinite number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that satisfies the original conditions when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39526a4fd8fa70a09be9251b26dbfb4bb423219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28credit_to_dskull16.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(credit_to_dskull16)\">Solution 2 (credit to dskull16)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (credit to dskull16)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by completing the square to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1f06202b3843fc9ab4bfab033c08d81a694a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + 2kn + n^2 - n^2 + m^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" />, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb92b26cc71fafb47fc682db6c061346e582d26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThen we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73bd3bac5de6be06408d474ca3312b0b8f0db852.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n)^2 + m^2 - n^2 = a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"21\" /> for some natural number a.\nThis then gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa048a31b3b075ab0ca0cd4a84d59e520337d0f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 - n^2 = a^2 - (k+n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"21\" /> which we can write like\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/8491b988ed8e99d2cefdd4f1876c07af3a3cf280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m+n)(m-n) = (a+k+n)(a-k-n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"331\" height=\"20\" /> by difference of two squares.\n</p><p><br />\nNow we remark that the left hand side is a constant since we prematurely chose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Acknowledging the fact that this equation is comprised entirely of integers, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174abf31458cb8953ab94e215bd6f9e411fba758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+k-n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e02aaeb02cd30db91c000289e53141c7f73a9c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-k-n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> need both be factors of the left hand side of which there are finitely many. This means that there are finitely many solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIf however the left hand side were 0, implying that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39526a4fd8fa70a09be9251b26dbfb4bb423219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/7/6877a41aad02af11b0ef57d1b0ec8b102bf2d6a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = -n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />, we would be able to find infinitely many integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e600cdc5160a13403babc1e03d54c885ab46fd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+k = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec4f3da4f422b2346efe86724c8a0aee1023fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" /> as required.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO\">2007 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213829\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 339/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1006/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 58/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11262/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.555      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%    6.555      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18408:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213829 and revision id 214391. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}